WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.700
<i>I never expected this to happen 
the day before my match.</i>

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.200
<i>Life never goes the way you'd expect.</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.320
<i>All right! I'll do my best tomorrow!</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.830
Wow, look at all these people!

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:27.540
Well, all the representatives of each age 
group from seven prefectures are here.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.300
But that number will be cut in half today.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.800
Listen up!

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.830
All the STC players will survive to the end!

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:36.800
Right!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.340
<i>Okay!</i>

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:40.650
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.560
Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.320
<i>Finish warming up by 7:30, then go for a run.</i>

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.820
<i>Get signed in before 8:30.</i>

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.830
U-18 boys, No. 30, Maruo Eiichiro.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.930
<i>Then have all my things ready, 
including notes, drinks, and a towel,</i>

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.960
<i>and be courtside no less than ten 
minutes before the match starts.</i>

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.740
<i>My first opponent, Yakabe Tadanori,</i>

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.720
<i>made the top eight in the Tokyo Junior and 
number 36 in the Kanto Junior ranking.</i>

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.870
<i>He's a baseliner whose weapons are his 
serve and his forehand flat shot.</i>

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.060
<i>I'll start by looking for a clue as to 
how to attack in his backhand slice,</i>

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.580
<i>which is easiest to read 
since he uses it often.</i>

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.480
<i>So far, everything is going as planned.</i>

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.110
<i>If anything isn't, it's...</i>

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:58.670
Okay, then...

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.030
Go out with me.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.650
<i>No, no!</i>

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.110
<i>I was planning to confess 
to her one day, anyway!</i>

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:08.290
<i>It was just a little sooner than planned, 
not totally unexpected!</i>

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.910
<i>If I think of it as one weight off 
my shoulders, it's a positive thing!</i>

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:18.050
<i>But Mike said romance mode and combat 
mode are on opposite ends of the spectrum.</i>

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.550
<i>I should switch gears.</i>

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.800
Hi.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.800
Nice to meet you.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.680
<i>Huh... He's taller than 
he looked in the video.</i>

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.370
The first round of the Kanto Junior 
Tennis Tournament will now begin.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.440
Three-set match. Yakabe to serve.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.940
Good luck.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.330
A Hero and Loud Cheers

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.850
<i>Just because some unexpected things 
happened doesn't mean I should rush.</i>

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:56.590
<i>I just have to use whatever data 
I have and play in my own way.</i>

00:03:58.940 --> 00:03:59.700
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.840
<i>He's not just tall, but strong, too!</i>

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.720
<i>He moved up?!</i>

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.690
15-love.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.100
Yes! That's one point!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.190
<i>Serve and volley!</i>

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.710
<i>So not only did he grow taller and stronger,</i>

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.980
<i>but he's also no longer a baseliner?</i>

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.610
<i>Or was that just a surprise attack?</i>

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.820
<i>Hang on...</i>

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.360
<i>Suddenly everything about 
this match is unexpected!</i>

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:26.240
<i>Should I reset all the data 
I had and start over?</i>

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.870
<i>He didn't use a topspin 
serve like that, either!</i>

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.540
<i>He moved up again!</i>

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.220
30-love.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.130
<i>Taking the time to create new expectations 
is slowing my response time.</i>

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.790
<i>So Yakabe-kun made use of 
his sudden growth spurt</i>

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.470
<i>to change to a serve-and-volley style.</i>

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.960
<i>Calm down. It's still his serve.</i>

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.040
<i>This isn't the time to rush things.</i>

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.480
<i>First, I need to erase as much of that 
video data from my mind as I can</i>

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.940
<i>and focus on watching him closely.</i>

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.030
<i>The addition of topspin shots to his serves</i>

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.910
<i>makes his flat shots seem to reach farther.</i>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.540
Yakabe Tadanori 
Maruo Eiichiro

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>But when I've cornered him, the only 
backhand shot he uses is a slice.</i>

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:24.040
<i>Maybe he's not confident in his 
topspin shots because he hasn't</i>

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.510
<i>used them much in matches yet.</i>

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.010
<i>Okay!</i>

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:32.640
Yakabe Tadanori 
Maruo Eiichiro

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.730
<i>I should use serves with high odds of success,</i>

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.640
<i>and not let him break!</i>

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.570
<i>When he moves up to volley,</i>

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.270
<i>he mostly relies on his 
strong forehand flat shot.</i>

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.530
<i>But that forehand shot isn't 
too different from the video.</i>

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.030
<i>His volley isn't bad,</i>

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.780
<i>but his stance is rigid and constrained.</i>

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.660
<i>That's probably a sign that he isn't used to it.</i>

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.220
<i>Even as a fellow serve-and-volley player, 
he'd be no match for Takuma-san.</i>

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.910
<i>So I can get past him!</i>

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.340
Love-15.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.420
Yeah!

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.590
<i>Backhand slice, forehand, and volley...</i>

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.930
<i>I'm starting to see what I should target.</i>

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:14.560
<i>I was shaken when I saw how much his 
physique and style had changed in a year,</i>

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.350
<i>but since the changes were so abrupt,</i>

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.860
<i>they've left a few weaknesses exposed.</i>

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.060
Yes!

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.690
<i>He's not unbeatable!</i>

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.580
Yes!

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.070
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.980
<i>He's going after my weak points, one by one!</i>

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:35.580
Yakabe Tadanori 
Maruo Eiichiro

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.320
Game, set, and match.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:50.090
Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-3, 6-0.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.050
Yes!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.840
<i>He's unseeded, like me,</i>

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.410
<i>but he's really strong.</i>

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.560
<i>All right! I made it past the first round!</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.490
Hey, good game.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.190
Oh, Aoi-san.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.140
Looks like you're in good shape.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:10.590
Yeah. I'm not even tired yet.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.150
Really? I guess it's about time, then.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.330
If things go right, you'll face Ide tomorrow.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:17.780
He might give you a bit of trouble.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.330
Okay.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.830
Matsuda Takahiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.580
40-15.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.860
One more point, Yosshi!

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:28.630
Focus!

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.880
Come on, Ide!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.150
Finish it here!

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.340
Game, set, and match.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.390
Winner: Ide.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.890
All right!

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.530
You did it, Yosshi!

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.770
Congrats!

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.150
Thanks!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.440
So now you're headed for the second round.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.780
If you win there, you can 
go to the nationals, right?

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.990
It's a big match.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.990
Yeah. I have to win tomorrow.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.750
I'm gonna go all-out!

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.370
You can do it, Yosshi!

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.610
Game, set, and match.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:06.380
Winner: Takasaki. Score: 6-1, 6-0.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.210
All right!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.130
Takasaki-san's doing amazing today, isn't she?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.060
She's even more fired up than usual.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.760
Congrats on getting past the first round!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.550
Oh, Ei-chan!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.140
I'm on top of my game in every way!

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.250
She's blinding me.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.070
<i>"In every way"...</i>

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.560
<i>Is she including me in that?</i>

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.320
<i>It'd sure make me happy if she is...</i>

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.950
<i>It's amazing that she can turn everything 
good that happens into a positive influence.</i>

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.990
Bro! I won, too!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.330
We're all done.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.420
Everyone here from STC has now 
made it through the first round!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.070
All right!

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:45.370
Looks like all the first round results are up.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.380
Everyone we expected to win, has won.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.050
Nabae Yu VS Yamashita Shinobu

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.050
<i>The first seed, Nabae-kun...</i>

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.220
Okada Takayuki VS Shima Kosuke

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.220
<i>The second seed, Okada-kun...</i>

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.430
Araya Hiroshi VS Baba Tetsuhiro

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.430
<i>The third seed, Araya-kun...</i>

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.930
Ide Yoshiaki VS Matsuda Takahiro

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.930
<i>And the fifth seed, who I'm 
playing tomorrow, Ide-kun.</i>

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.710
Huh? Since when are you two going out?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:12.490
Huh?!

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.680
Yeah, since yesterday.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:16.070
Y-Yeah...

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:19.210
Wow, really? Congratulations!

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.620
Seems like it was a long time coming.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.290
You mean you guys haven't 
been a couple all this time?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.010
W-Wait, yesterday?!

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.760
Welcome back, Bro.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.340
You were gone a while.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.410
Yeah... I went for a walk 
and ended up at the beach.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.980
The beach, huh?

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.300
If we win tomorrow, want to light fireworks?

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.010
Sounds good!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.030
What, that's when it happened?!

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.640
W-Well, yeah...

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.290
What's the big deal?

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.440
They're both playing well.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.100
Don't get so mad, Yukichi.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.260
But that was right before 
the first round! That's...

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.680
That's not right!

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.650
I-I can't help that.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.180
Idiot!

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:54.900
Ow!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.030
That's what you get for taking 
our Nat-chan for yourself!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.990
Hey, where's Yosshi?

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:10.540
He said he was going for a run 
around the venue to warm up.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.900
I'm gonna show 'em today!

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.690
Ow! It hurts!

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.690
Hey! Are you okay?

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.540
The kid jumped out of nowhere!

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.270
That doesn't matter! We need an ambulance!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.940
Hey, what's going on?

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.930
A kid got hit by a car!

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:30.680
Wait, isn't that Ide?

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:31.650
It is!

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.030
Hang in there. An ambulance 
will be here soon, okay?

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.930
I need an ambulance, please!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.250
A child's been hit by a car!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.030
The location is—

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.660
Hey, Ei-chan! We came to cheer you on!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.280
Kageyama! Sasaki-san!

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.910
Thanks for coming all this way.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.650
It's no problem.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.540
<i>Well, it's fine with me, since 
I'm thinking of it as a date.</i>

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.170
Only for today, though. 
We have to go back tonight.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.360
How's it going?

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.170
It's going great!

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.590
Of course it is. You're brimming 
with happiness, after all.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:03.870
Huh? What's that mean?

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:06.190
Um, Yukichi-kun?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.850
You shouldn't keep secrets 
from your best friends.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:11.850
What is it?

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:16.120
Well, actually... I'm going 
out with Nat-chan now.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:23.240
I was planning to tell you guys 
after my match, honest!

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:28.250
Well, not that it matters to me, 
since tennis is my girlfriend.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.890
S-Sorry! I'm actually still warming up, too.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.000
Later, okay?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.760
Oh... Sure, later.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:40.260
<i>Sorry, Ei-chan. I can't be happy 
about this right now, either.</i>

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.760
It hurts! It hurts!

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.210
It's okay. The doctor's going 
to look at you right now.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.560
He'll make it stop hurting 
before you know it, okay?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.270
Would you hold my hand the whole time?

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:54.350
Sure.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.520
I'll stay right here. Hang in there!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.780
It hurts... It hurts!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:00.730
Hang in there.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.850
He'll need surgery.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:03.230
What?!

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.280
Surgery?!

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.790
I don't want surgery!

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.060
Yes, but...

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:12.360
Hey, you know... I actually 
have a tennis match today.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:16.290
Tennis? You're a tennis player?

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.390
Sort of.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:23.680
It's a big match that will determine 
whether I'll be able to go pro someday.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.290
Will you promise me something?

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.060
I swear I'll win my match today,

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.430
so you have to get through that surgery.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.150
O-Okay.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.830
<i>My opponent today is Ide Yoshiaki-kun.</i>

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.790
<i>He made the top eight at the 
All-Japan Indoor Invitational.</i>

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:46.980
<i>He's inconsistent, but he's shown results 
on a level equal to Araya-kun's.</i>

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:47.950
<i>And...</i>

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:51.040
You should probably pay 
more attention to Ide.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:53.100
Ide is a rather unusual player.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:53.790
Huh?

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.540
I don't understand it at all,

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.540
but when there's a large, enthusiastic crowd,

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:03.050
or if he's up against a tough opponent 
or one he has a history with,

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.300
or if it's a point that's absolutely critical...

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:11.330
The point is that when he has to perform, 
he shows incredible ability.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:18.200
I believe that he has the kind of 
spirit seen in many top athletes.

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:21.580
Though, his technique isn't as impressive.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:27.320
So if I have to play Ide, I would 
want to avoid a close match.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.080
If I want to win, I need 
to dominate him early on.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.690
<i>Even Nabae-kun said he wouldn't 
want a close match against him.</i>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.880
<i>He won't be easy to beat, of course.</i>

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.220
<i>But if I don't win in the second round,</i>

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:42.960
<i>I can't advance to the All-Japan Junior.</i>

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:46.850
<i>And if that happens, I have 
to give up on going pro.</i>

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.970
<i>All right! I'm ready!</i>

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.240
<i>Five minutes until we start!</i>

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:55.230
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.300
Ei-chan! Ei-chan!

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.500
Kageyama? What's wrong?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.390
My match is about to start.

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:05.940
There's some big trouble 
with your next match!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.200
Huh?

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.810
Please!

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.040
He'll be here soon!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.810
So many people...

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.190
Did something happen?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:26.550
Apparently your opponent, Ide, isn't here yet.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:29.930
They say there was a traffic accident 
near where he was warming up.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.980
What?! No way!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:34.690
Is Ide-kun... o-okay?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:38.190
Yeah, he wasn't actually hurt at all,

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.230
but he went to the hospital 
with the kid who got hurt and

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.990
had to tell the police what happened,

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.940
so it looks like he won't make it 
here in time for the match.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.050
No way...

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:53.300
So his friends are asking the tournament 
referee to delay the start of the match.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:56.160
He just left the hospital, 
and he's on his way here!

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.120
He says the kid's gonna be okay.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.110
Oh, good!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:04.170
His email said he can be here in 
twenty—no, thirty minutes!

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.190
Oh, Maruo-kun.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:07.960
Yes?

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:11.010
I was just about to call for you.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.570
It seems Ide-kun is running late.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.970
Yeah, I heard the gist of the story.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.990
I talked to the hospital staff and the police,

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.600
and they said he was a 
tremendous help to them.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.730
Given the circumstances, 
if it's all right with you,

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.550
I'd like to wait for Ide-kun to get 
here before starting the match.

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:28.480
What do you think?

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.720
Oh... Yes. I think that would be best.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.240
Thank you so much!

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.910
Oh, good! Now Yosshi will be able to play!

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.420
He's such an idiot.

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:41.170
One wrong move and he'd have lost by default.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.380
He's lucky his opponent's a nice guy.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.680
He's worked so hard, saying the 
next All-Japan Junior is his last.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.630
Would he throw all that away 
for some kid he doesn't know?

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.100
Now that you mention it, in middle school,

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:55.310
he was late for school once because 
he was looking after an abandoned cat.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.390
Well, that's the kind of guy he is.

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:03.070
I bet he was hurting even more 
than the kid he was with.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:05.030
I can totally see that!

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:10.650
It's remarkable that he would prioritize 
an injured child over an big match.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.860
Well, not many people could do that.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.360
And his friends have such faith in him.

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.540
Sheesh...

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:21.680
Why do things always turn out 
like this when he's involved?

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.290
Okada-kun...

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:26.340
Whenever something happens 
and turns into a big deal,

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.160
he always ends up being 
the hero of the story.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.060
This has gotten pretty crazy, huh?

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:32.740
Yeah.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>But Okada-kun is right.</i>

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:40.410
<i>I already feel like I'm being 
pulled into Ide-kun's story.</i>

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:43.440
<i>I have to keep my head on straight.</i>

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:49.470
I feel like such an idiot.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.250
You are not.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.750
But you could sort of sense it, couldn't you?

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.070
Sh-Shut up!

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.520
<i>So that's how it is...</i>

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:01.330
Huh? Something seems weird.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:05.330
Aren't there too many people at this court?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:09.600
Maybe some people came to watch 
after hearing about what Ide did.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:12.380
He seemed to have a lot 
of fans to begin with.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.770
You mean most of these people 
will be rooting for the other guy?

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:18.470
Gives me a bad feeling...

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.030
In terms of skill alone,

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:24.640
I think Maruo has reached Ide's level,

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.400
but they say Ide is strong 
when the heat is on.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.480
He's probably used to matches 
where he's in the spotlight, too.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.610
That makes it hard to figure 
how this match will go.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:37.340
It'll be a different kind of match 
from what Maruo's used to.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.150
<i>It's been thirty minutes already?</i>

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:41.490
<i>But still...</i>

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.000
<i>I can't believe how many people are here.</i>

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:51.260
Hey, isn't that Yosshi?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:52.380
Where? Where?

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.010
Oh! It is!

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.360
He's finally here!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.030
Hey! Yosshi!

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:58.030
Hey!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.410
Over here!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.880
Oh, so that's the famous Ide?

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:05.430
I heard he almost lost by default 
for a kid who was in an accident.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.740
Seriously? The fifth seed did that?

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:08.790
That's awesome!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.310
Let's go watch!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.220
I... I'm here!

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:18.320
<i>He's here!</i>

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.960
Thanks, guys!

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.140
Wait, why are there so many people here?

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.180
They heard about you and 
came to cheer you on!

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.710
Huh? Me?

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:29.540
The kid was okay, right?

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:34.460
Yeah. He'll need surgery, 
but they said it's not that bad.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.420
Thank goodness!

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:40.550
But he kept crying, and the police 
kept me for ages. It was rough.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.530
Anyway, it worked out great.

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:44.590
You get to play your match!

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.670
Yeah! You worked so hard,

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.100
and you were so close to losing by default!

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:53.460
Well, it worked out, right? 
Thanks to you guys.

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.390
Idiot!

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:55.940
Sorry, okay?

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.610
Here's your stuff.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.860
Just hurry up and get going!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.870
Make sure you win!

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:04.660
Yep!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.120
There he is!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.680
Ide! I'm rooting for you!

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:12.750
The All-Japan Junior won't 
be any fun without you!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.750
Do your best for that little hurt kid, too!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.700
Wow, we're totally the away team here.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.260
I-It's crazy.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:25.390
<i>It'll depend on whether he can 
play without getting bewildered.</i>

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.910
Sorry, Maruo-kun. Thanks for waiting!

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:32.350
It's okay. I'm glad you get to play.

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:35.330
I'll get ready right now. 
Just give me a sec.

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.550
<i>Amazing... All this attention is on him,</i>

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:42.240
<i>and he's not nervous at all.</i>

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.740
<i>He must be used to large audiences.</i>

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:49.500
<i>No, he's the type that actually plays 
better under those circumstances.</i>

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.030
You have three minutes to practice.

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:56.880
<i>That means this situation 
works in Ide-kun's favor.</i>

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.500
<i>Not only that,</i>

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.510
<i>but the skill of his shots is enough 
to compete on a national level.</i>

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:07.250
<i>And I have to beat an opponent 
like this, in a situation like this.</i>

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.660
<i>Isn't that...</i>

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.500
<i>sort of like a professional match?</i>

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:14.770
Time.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:17.540
I won't forget my debt to you.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:19.090
Don't worry about that.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.690
I heard what happened.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:24.530
Really? It was pretty rough, to be honest.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.840
But it all worked out, thanks 
to you and everyone else.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.580
It must be fate that I get to play like this!

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:35.210
Let's make this the best match ever!

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:41.650
Y-Yeah!

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:48.270
The second round of the Kanto Junior 
Tennis Tournament will now begin.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:51.350
Three-set match. Ide to serve.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:55.100
<i>"Let's make this the best match ever," huh?</i>

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.620
<i>Yeah, let's. So we won't regret anything.</i>

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:03.110
<i>Because this might be the last 
time I put my all on the line</i>

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.120
<i>for a tennis match.</i>

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.010
<i>But I'm sure it's the same for Ide-kun.</i>

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.250
<i>I want to win a match like this!</i>

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.040
You can do it, Yosshi!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.380
Yosshi! Get the first point!

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.300
Love-15.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.230
All right! Nice return, Ei-chan!

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:37.200
Um, guys? Can't you cheer for him out loud?

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.810
Looks like he's not unnecessarily nervous.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.190
<i>With Ide-kun, victory goes to the swiftest!</i>

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:46.040
<i>I need to take the lead and try not to let 
him make this a close, exciting match!</i>

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:48.410
Ide! Get that point this time!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.580
<i>For a topspin shot, that was fast!</i>

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:53.840
Yes!

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:55.060
15-all.

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:56.790
Yeah! Nice serve!

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.230
Ide! Get your second point!

00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.200
Awesome!

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:01.210
You're awesome, Ide!

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:04.460
<i>Wow, the cheering is insane.</i>

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.470
Quiet, please!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:08.530
Okay, Ide! Take the lead!

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:09.930
Hold on to it!

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.470
Okay...

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:12.370
Nice, Ide!

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:13.060
One more point!

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.470
Ide's incredible!

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.790
What the heck is this?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:04.360
It's pretty hard to play when everyone's 
cheering for my opponent.

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:06.170
If he's only going for decisive shots,

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:09.010
I'll just have to use my 
best method to hold serve!

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:09.700
Here goes!

00:24:09.700 --> 00:24:13.010
His serves weren't this fast last year.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.330
He's totally different from 
when I saw him play Nabae.

00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:16.370
Oops...

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:17.870
I'll think about it while I play.

00:24:17.870 --> 00:24:20.000
I'll figure something out eventually.

00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:22.560
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Whish, Then Fwoom

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:23.850
"Whish, Then Fwoom."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:34.000
End
